<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ma'add</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ma'add was a confederation of tribes of central and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> in late antiquity. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-arabia">South Arabian</a> inscriptions of the 4th to 6th centuries record Himyarite campaigns against Ma'add, and the Himyarite kings set the Kindite house over them to control the interior. Later Arab genealogists made Ma'add, son of Adnan, the ancestor of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a>.</p></div>
